      "body": "Slice 1 of the note→board sharing model for #7587 (decision record on #5830): the data model.\n\n- `Post` gains an optional `note_ref: NoteRef` — note object id, home server, pinned version id + content hash, sharer attribution. The post stores a reference, never note content (the reference-not-content invariant everything else hangs on).\n- Back-compat: `note_ref` is `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]`; v1 post bodies written before this field decode as `None` (covered by a test).\n- Authority: a note reference must be signed by its named sharer (attribution cannot be forged either direction). The note target is deliberately NOT a graph dependency — it lives on its home server, so insertion never requires it and replication closure never claims it.\n- Edges: `BoardGraph::note_embeds()` projects every post —embeds→ note edge in deterministic hash order; `BoardGraph::note_backlinks(note)` returns the posts sharing a note. (Full backlink query surface / jump-through parity is Slice 3.)\n\nTests: `cargo test -p id-core boards::` — 36 passed (4 new: embeds edge to an absent note, sharer-must-sign both directions, shape rejects bad sharer / empty home server, v1 body without `note_ref` decodes as `None`). `cargo check -p id-core --all-targets --all-features` passes (one pre-existing `residency.rs` missing-docs warning). Local clippy was unavailable in this worktree's toolchain and the full `id` check needs the built `web/dist` assets; CI's id checks cover both.\n\nRemaining on #7587 (task 14142 tracks them): Slice 2 — live/pinned views + reply anchoring (exact/relocated/orphaned); Slice 3 — backlink parity + attributed changelog events; Slice 4 — cross-server grant-checked, hash-verified resolution + two-server E2E.\n\nRefs #7587, #5830.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796791714&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7953&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7953&signature=aaa207e8de43d24a68da6263d827db90407c6735a28900de8281259bb658f872\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7953?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
